# 3. Governance Principles

## Purpose

The governance principles establish the fundamental engineering rules that guide the management of all System Objectives within the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA).

These principles ensure consistency, traceability, and disciplined engineering throughout the objective lifecycle.

---

## Governance Principles

### GP-01 — Objectives Before Solutions

System Objectives shall define **what** the system must achieve and shall not prescribe **how** those objectives are to be implemented.

---

### GP-02 — Solution Independence

All System Objectives shall remain independent of specific technologies, components, algorithms, or implementation methods unless explicitly governed by a higher-level engineering decision.

---

### GP-03 — Complete Traceability

Every System Objective shall maintain traceable relationships to its parent authority, related objectives, derived requirements, verification activities, and validation activities.

---

### GP-04 — Controlled Evolution

System Objectives shall evolve only through a controlled engineering review and approval process. All changes shall preserve historical traceability.

---

### GP-05 — Consistency

All objective documentation shall follow the governance framework, identification standards, and documentation structures defined by this document.

---

### GP-06 — Explicit Authority

Authority governing every System Objective shall be explicitly declared and traceable. No objective shall exist without an identified governing authority.

---

### GP-07 — Engineering Integrity

Engineering decisions affecting System Objectives shall be based on objective evidence, scientific principles, engineering analysis, and documented rationale.

---

### GP-08 — Constraints Guide Innovation

Engineering constraints shall be recognized as fundamental inputs that guide innovation, objective development, and system evolution rather than being treated solely as limitations.

---

### GP-09 — Lifecycle Governance

Every System Objective shall be governed throughout its entire lifecycle, from creation to retirement, under a documented and controlled process.

---

### GP-10 — Continuous Improvement

The governance framework shall support continuous learning and improvement while preserving repository stability, engineering discipline, and configuration integrity.
